  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD017531",
    "title": "Interaction mapping of human condensin I and condensin II complexes using DSBU-cross-linking and mass spectrometry",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Human condensin I and condensin II complexes play essential roles in chromatin condensation during the cell division process. Both complexes use ATP as the energy source to pack extended chromatin into the short form of chromosome. In order to understand the mechanism of their function, we performed cross-linking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) analyses of both complexes and mapped the inter-molecular and intra-molecular interactions of the subunits.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Human condensin I and condensin II complexes were expressed and purified from insect cells. Purified complexes were cross-linked with DSBU (disuccinimidyl dibutyric urea), precipitated, and digested with Lys-C and trypsin. Digested peptides were desalted and fractionated by size-exclusion chromatography prior to the analysis with a Q-Exactive Plus. All fractions were analysed with a standard MS-MS/MS top 10 method.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Raw data from the Q-Exactive Plus were converted to MGF (Mascot generic files) format with program msConvert GUI from ProteoWizard Toolkit version 3. Program MeroX version 1.6.6.6  was used for cross-link identification.",
